<table width="100%" cellspacing="2" cellpadding="0" border="0" bgcolor="#d0d0d0">
	<tr>
		<td><span style="font:bold 14pt Arial"><i>Holy Order of Tunare Guild Charter</i></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td><span class="stdtext"><br><i>The Holy Order of Tunare is an internet guild based on the
		MMORPG, <a href="http://www.everquest.com">EverQuest</a>.  The Holy Order of Tunare is situated
		on the <a href="http://www.bristlebane.com">Bristlebane</a> server and strives to promote honor,
		valor, chivalry, loyalty, camaraderie, and most importantly, family-like relationships.
		The Holy Order of Tunare is a good guild and allows membership to those that are good
		aligned in character. All players wishing to become a brethren or sister of this guild
		will be considered due to their deity and individual merits. The Holy Order of Tunare
		shall be strong as long as our reputation and family remains filled with honor. </i></span>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td><span class="stdtext"><br><b>Guild Guidelines</b></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td><span class="stdtext"><br>
		<ul>
			<li>The guidelines of the Holy Order of Tunare are simple. The lands of Norrath
			require strong teamwork to succeed so our guild charter reflects that aspect. The guild
			is broken down into different Divisions, each being led by a Marshall
			who oversees the entire division. A representative from each branch reports back
			to the Marshall, to ensure that needs are being met. </li>
			<li>In general, the members of the Holy Order of Tunare should be available to help
			members whenever there is a need for help. However, there may be instances that
			teleportation is not available, it is somewhat unfair to ask a fellow brother or
			sister to rush from the lands of Antonica to Luclin at the blink of an eye. We believe
			this to be a sound principle, and hope that it can be achieved whenever possible.</li>
			<li>Communication with other members of the guild is the basis for our strength
			and camaraderie. If you see a fellow brother or sister, please make sure you acknowledge
			them.</li>
			<li>The Holy Order of Tunare has a broad base of membership and currently has a minimum
			level requirement of 12 in order to join. Therefore it is tasked onto the brothers and
			sisters to always help the less fortunate of our family. Your help and support help
			make our family strong.</li>
			<li>It is asked that each member of the Holy Order of Tunare family will help each other
			with quests. It is considered a noble act when helping someone gain further knowledge
			or an item that will enhance his or her experience in the beautiful lands of Norrath.
			Besides that, it is an act of unselfishness and will promote good esteem with other
			members of the family.</li>
			<li>Events are planned as often as possible and your participation in them is greatly
			appreciated. Most events are planned with most age ranges in mind and your ideas for
			events are always welcomed.</li>
			<li>Remember, the success of the Holy Order of Tunare lies within all of you. We are a
			family, and with our strong bonds we shall always live in Norrath.</li>
			<li>Our guild charter and guidelines are living documents and may change at any time.
			If you have suggestions or comments, please pass them on to <a href="mailto:holyorderoftunare@hotmail.com">Lady Siniana D'artanian</a>,
			Earl Marshall and Guild Leader of the Holy Order of Tunare.</li>
		</ul>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td><span class="stdtext"><br><b>Recruiting Requirements and Guidelines</b></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td><span class="stdtext"><br>The Holy Order of Tunare is a role-playing based guild on the <a href="http://www.bristlebane.com">Bristlebane</a> server as part
		of the MMORPG, <a href="http://www.everquest.com">EverQuest</a>. The Holy Order of Tunare is not only a group of gamers, but also
		a group of online friends, who enjoy each other’s company and presence. Each person wanting
		to be a member of our family will be given an equal chance of membership.
		<p>Therefore, we present to you the requirements and guidelines for membership into the Holy Order of Tunare. </p>
			<ol>
				<li>Persons wishing to join the Holy Order may apply after obtaining rank in their 12th season.</li>
				<li>The following deities are ones that we believe to have good alignment, and therefore will be
				granted membership into our guild:
					<ul>
						<li>The Tribunal</li>
						<li>Rodcet Nife</li>
						<li>Quellious</li>
						<li>Mithaniel Marr</li>
						<li>Karana</li>
						<li>Erollisi Marr</li>
						<li>Brell Serilis</li>
						<li>Bristlebane</li>
						<li>Agnostic</li>
						<li>Prexus</li>
					</ul>
					A screenshot showing the deity will be necessary to prove your faith as well.
				</li>
				<li>To apply, please use the application form. You will be contacted as soon as the
				application has been received and reviewed. You may also apply by sending a message
				to Lady Siniana D'artanian or by posting a message in the New Recruits section of
				our message board.</li>
				<li>Lady Siniana D’artanian, Earl Marshall and Guild Leader, will contact you with a
				scroll shortly thereafter. Enclosed will be an application for membership into
				the Holy Order of Tunare with the character you listed. </li>
				<li>Please fill out the application candidly and return it is as soon as possible.
				Thereafter, the Earl Marshall will review your application.</li>
				<li>After review of your application, you will receive a scroll stating whether or not
				it was received and the status of your application. The Earl Marshall will also update
				your status in the Recruits forum of the message tree, so check there for more
				details.</li>
				<li>After careful review, it will be necessary that the recruit seek out three
				members of the guild and get their approvals. These members will then post that
				they have spoken with you and therefore vouch for your character. </li>
				<li>Once the three or more vouchers have been confirmed. The recruit will then be
				considered for initiation into the guild if they meet all of the guild guidelines
				and standards. The Holy Order is not concerned with quantities, rather, we consider
				ourselves proud of the quality of our membership.</li>
				<li>The recruit, if accepted will be given a one-month probation into the guild.
				If, after the one-month probation period, the guild does not feel comfortable with
				you, then you shall be removed and have to apply again within thirty days. If you
				are acceptable, then you shall be allowed to continue as a Brother or Sister of
				the Holy Order. </li>
				<li>At any time during the recruitment process, the Earl Marshall can make a decision
				as to whether or not you will be allowed into the guild. If there is something from
				the past or that is demonstrated by current behavior that is not behooving to the
				guild, your application will be denied.</li>
			</ol>
		</span>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td><span class="stdtext">If you have any questions about the recruitment process, please
		contact Lady Siniana D’artanian in Norrath or at <a href="mailto:holyorderoftunare@hotmail.com">holyorderoftunare@hotmail.com</a>.</span>
		</td>
	</tr>
